  m_Name: 7 - Game Speed
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: UtilityScriptIWrite::HintSO
  hintId: tutorial_game_speed
  isUnlockedByDefault: 1
  ignoreLock: 0
  title: Game Speed
  image: {fileID: 0}
  description: '<b>Game Speed</b>


    Game Speed controls how fast animations and
    program execution are displayed.


    You can adjust the animation speed to
    make robot actions and environmental events play faster or slower.


    You
    can also change the Step Delay, which determines the amount of time between each
    instruction during execution.


    Lower Step Delay values make the program
    execute more quickly, while higher values make it easier to observe instructions
    one step at a time.


    Adjusting Game Speed can help with debugging, learning
    program flow, and speeding up repetitive tasks.'
  isImageBig: 0
